568
00:27:16,290 --> 00:27:17,570
I don't think so, Nine.

569
00:27:17,780 --> 00:27:19,240
I could never compare to you.

570
00:27:19,800 --> 00:27:20,790
I think Third...

571
00:27:20,840 --> 00:27:22,560
has the best partner in the world.

572
00:27:23,500 --> 00:27:24,030
Mm...

573
00:27:24,050 --> 00:27:26,150
He's so lucky to have you as his partner.

574
00:27:27,110 --> 00:27:28,270
Then...

575
00:27:30,880 --> 00:27:33,000
can I ask you a straight question?

576
00:27:34,660 --> 00:27:37,690
What are your feelings toward Third

577
00:27:39,400 --> 00:27:40,400
right now?

578
00:27:44,590 --> 00:27:45,790
Is it still the same?

579
00:27:54,770 --> 00:27:55,430
So that means

580
00:27:55,450 --> 00:27:57,430
what he's doing to you is working.

581
00:27:59,700 --> 00:28:00,780
Because today,

582
00:28:00,910 --> 00:28:02,860
Third told me that he liked you,

583
00:28:03,780 --> 00:28:05,460
that you seemed natural,

584
00:28:06,160 --> 00:28:08,300
and that it'd work out great
if you guys were partners.

585
00:28:10,460 --> 00:28:11,160
See?

586
00:28:11,500 --> 00:28:12,920
That means Third

587
00:28:13,520 --> 00:28:15,890
is trying to drive a wedge
between you and me.

588
00:28:17,730 --> 00:28:18,710
How about this?

589
00:28:19,890 --> 00:28:21,480
If you don't want us to fight,

590
00:28:21,760 --> 00:28:23,970
try to keep your distance from him.

591
00:28:25,720 --> 00:28:27,890
The reason I'm having
this conversation with you today,

592
00:28:28,360 --> 00:28:29,300
warning you,

593
00:28:29,320 --> 00:28:30,240
is that...

594
00:28:31,210 --> 00:28:32,300
I'm sure...

595
00:28:32,900 --> 00:28:34,270
you wouldn't lie,

596
00:28:34,890 --> 00:28:36,080
betray me,

597
00:28:36,740 --> 00:28:38,560
or hurt me.

598
00:28:39,880 --> 00:28:41,010
Rest assured.

599
00:28:41,250 --> 00:28:42,390
I'll do everything I can

600
00:28:42,410 --> 00:28:44,090
to help you succeed, Nine,

601
00:28:44,520 --> 00:28:46,720
because I'm your fanboy.

602
00:28:48,620 --> 00:28:49,690
Thanks,

603
00:28:50,250 --> 00:28:52,010
my No. 1 fanboy.

604
00:28:55,690 --> 00:28:56,800
So what do you think?

605
00:29:00,420 --> 00:29:01,940
I think I believe him.

606
00:29:03,800 --> 00:29:05,270
I only got to know Third recently, too.

607
00:29:05,290 --> 00:29:06,660
Helping or coaching me

608
00:29:06,880 --> 00:29:08,820
doesn't mean
he's actually nice to me, yeah?

609
00:29:09,200 --> 00:29:10,690
Hey... think it through.

610
00:29:10,710 --> 00:29:12,430
You just got to know Nine, too, didn't you?

611
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:13,850
Like...

612
00:29:13,870 --> 00:29:16,830
getting to know him
as an actor you like and as a coworker

613
00:29:16,850 --> 00:29:18,030
are two different things.

614
00:29:18,290 --> 00:29:19,540
Are you taking your fave's side?

615
00:29:19,760 --> 00:29:20,320
Ugh!

616
00:29:20,340 --> 00:29:21,780
And you're not?

617
00:29:21,800 --> 00:29:22,840
You put him on a pedestal,

618
00:29:22,860 --> 00:29:24,240
praising him like he's some deity.

619
00:29:25,440 --> 00:29:26,140
Hey,

620
00:29:26,550 --> 00:29:27,470
Wan.

621
00:29:27,490 --> 00:29:30,100
I really think you need to slow down
and use your brain.

622
00:29:30,120 --> 00:29:32,180
I know you're not that dumb.

623
00:29:34,670 --> 00:29:36,670
Why are you digressing?

624
00:29:37,090 --> 00:29:38,400
Just say you're taking Third's side.

625
00:29:38,960 --> 00:29:40,920
I'm not taking his side!

626
00:29:41,360 --> 00:29:43,510
But I genuinely believe
Third's a good person.

627
00:29:44,110 --> 00:29:45,980
I don't know if I can believe that.

628
00:29:47,030 --> 00:29:50,000
Lately, Third's been
coming around me differently, too.

629
00:29:50,800 --> 00:29:51,950
Him coming around you

630
00:29:51,970 --> 00:29:53,220
doesn't mean

631
00:29:53,250 --> 00:29:55,140
he's gonna hurt Nine or you, right?

632
00:29:55,390 --> 00:29:57,230
If Nine and Third
don't like each other's guts,

633
00:29:57,250 --> 00:29:58,730
then it's their business, isn't it?

634
00:29:58,750 --> 00:30:00,470
Let's say you were close to Third,

635
00:30:00,900 --> 00:30:02,260
and they're really on bad terms.

636
00:30:02,570 --> 00:30:04,500
It doesn't mean you have to
take anyone's side, right?

637
00:30:06,730 --> 00:30:07,690
I don't know.

638
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:08,570
You...

639
00:30:08,590 --> 00:30:10,500
have to observe and see how it goes.

640
00:30:11,080 --> 00:30:12,570
Anyone can say
whatever they want, no?

641
00:30:12,590 --> 00:30:14,700
Everybody wants
to look good in the eyes of others.

642
00:30:14,820 --> 00:30:15,410
You,

643
00:30:15,430 --> 00:30:16,870
just be sweet.

644
00:30:16,890 --> 00:30:18,860
Don't judge him
based on other people's words.

645
00:30:19,050 --> 00:30:20,080
Sure!

646
00:30:20,470 --> 00:30:21,470
Yes, Mom!

647
00:30:22,940 --> 00:30:25,030
It's okay to be careful,
but don't be paranoid.

648
00:30:25,060 --> 00:30:26,580
That's gonna wreck you,
I'll tell you that.

649
00:30:27,450 --> 00:30:28,610
Now, go to sleep.

650
00:30:28,640 --> 00:30:30,000
Aren't you on location tomorrow?

651
00:30:30,020 --> 00:30:30,450
Mm.

652
00:30:30,470 --> 00:30:31,980
Go sleep properly!

653
00:30:39,200 --> 00:30:39,960
Catch!

654
00:30:43,070 --> 00:30:46,080
[Shooting Day]
[The Deep Between Us Q2]

655
00:30:47,170 --> 00:30:48,170
Oh?

656
00:30:48,310 --> 00:30:49,960
You're always early.

657
00:30:50,400 --> 00:30:51,590
Good. How consistent of you.

658
00:30:51,620 --> 00:30:52,730
But I've taught you before, right?

659
00:30:52,750 --> 00:30:55,310
Didn't I teach you
the Exclusive Star 102 course?

660
00:30:55,570 --> 00:30:57,480
Tell me, when you become famous,

661
00:30:57,790 --> 00:30:58,720
what will you do, sweetie?

662
00:30:58,780 --> 00:31:00,210
You have to be late

663
00:31:00,320 --> 00:31:02,970
so that the other cast and crew
move mountains for you.

664
00:31:02,990 --> 00:31:04,200
I'm using the 101 course.

665
00:31:04,220 --> 00:31:04,950
I spent the night here.

666
00:31:04,970 --> 00:31:05,460
You're kidding!

667
00:31:05,480 --> 00:31:06,880
Someone like you spending the night?

668
00:31:06,900 --> 00:31:08,170
Not buying it!

669
00:31:08,780 --> 00:31:09,270
I'm gonna go.

670
00:31:09,290 --> 00:31:10,960
See you. I'm gonna go have a meal.

671
00:31:10,980 --> 00:31:12,470
Yeah, run along.

672
00:31:12,490 --> 00:31:13,880
Run along. Has Pai arrived?

673
00:31:14,910 --> 00:31:16,640
Wow, that boy. He ignored me.

674
00:31:16,690 --> 00:31:18,780
- If I arrive after him, I'll get yelled at!
- He has this side to him?

675
00:31:21,150 --> 00:31:22,360
- Hello, Jern.
- Oh?

676
00:31:22,790 --> 00:31:24,180
Hi there.

677
00:31:24,210 --> 00:31:25,590
- Uh...
- You're here early.

678
00:31:25,610 --> 00:31:26,170
Right...

679
00:31:26,730 --> 00:31:27,570
Uh...

680
00:31:28,090 --> 00:31:29,690
You and Third are close?

681
00:31:30,570 --> 00:31:31,100
Not really.

682
00:31:32,280 --> 00:31:33,560
Sike!

683
00:31:33,580 --> 00:31:34,980
We're close. Why?

684
00:31:35,200 --> 00:31:36,030
Uh...

685
00:31:36,580 --> 00:31:38,360
I just wanna know.

686
00:31:38,600 --> 00:31:39,890
What kind of person is he?

687
00:31:41,040 --> 00:31:42,060
He's nice,

688
00:31:42,080 --> 00:31:43,480
but boy, is he blunt.

689
00:31:43,740 --> 00:31:45,880
Whatever he thinks, he speaks.

690
00:31:45,900 --> 00:31:46,620
Sometimes...

691
00:31:46,640 --> 00:31:47,630
he even chews people out.

692
00:31:47,650 --> 00:31:48,540
You know that, sweetie!

693
00:31:49,300 --> 00:31:51,560
Actually, I don't like
gossiping or anything,

694
00:31:52,040 --> 00:31:53,450
but there's more to spill!

695
00:31:54,110 --> 00:31:56,290
Third is punctual.

696
00:31:56,320 --> 00:31:57,540
He's easy to work with,

697
00:31:57,780 --> 00:31:58,990
except for one thing, sweetie.

698
00:31:59,010 --> 00:32:00,120
He likes asking,

699
00:32:00,140 --> 00:32:00,870
asking,

700
00:32:00,890 --> 00:32:01,560
and asking!

701
00:32:01,580 --> 00:32:03,140
So much so that he goes on and on

702
00:32:03,170 --> 00:32:04,550
and on and on and on and on.

703
00:32:05,580 --> 00:32:06,260
But that's good...

704
00:32:06,280 --> 00:32:08,000
By the time
he comes on set, he's good to go.

705
00:32:08,170 --> 00:32:09,290
Isn't that right, sweetie?

706
00:32:09,930 --> 00:32:11,810
- It is.
- Meanwhile, some actors...

707
00:32:11,830 --> 00:32:12,890
don't even memorize their lines,

708
00:32:12,910 --> 00:32:13,650
and when they're on set,

709
00:32:13,670 --> 00:32:14,910
I don't even know if they're gonna act.

710
00:32:16,690 --> 00:32:17,450
They just snap, snap,

711
00:32:17,470 --> 00:32:18,360
snap, snap, snap,

712
00:32:18,570 --> 00:32:19,190
and snap nonstop!

713
00:32:19,210 --> 00:32:21,020
How about I chop it off
if you're not doing your job?

714
00:32:21,040 --> 00:32:22,420
Not even memorizing the script.

715
00:32:23,230 --> 00:32:24,720
The reason I was hired

716
00:32:24,750 --> 00:32:26,190
is to run the set,

717
00:32:26,220 --> 00:32:28,040
not the other ten fucking things!

718
00:32:28,170 --> 00:32:29,400
Am I doing the work of a kraken?

719
00:32:29,420 --> 00:32:30,710
Ten shits just to get paid for one.

720
00:32:32,980 --> 00:32:33,860
You're... catching stray bullets?

721
00:32:33,880 --> 00:32:34,890
Wow, a whole cartridge.

722
00:32:35,620 --> 00:32:36,500
No...

723
00:32:36,520 --> 00:32:37,690
I'm just speaking generally.

724
00:32:37,710 --> 00:32:39,290
- Oh... okay.
- Just in general.

725
00:32:39,310 --> 00:32:39,870
In general!

726
00:32:39,890 --> 00:32:40,470
Totally general.

727
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:41,620
Sweetie,

728
00:32:41,640 --> 00:32:42,760
ask away if you don't get it.

729
00:32:42,780 --> 00:32:44,070
- Alright.
- Ask a bunch.

730
00:32:44,090 --> 00:32:44,950
A bunch.

731
00:32:48,550 --> 00:32:49,370
Okay.

732
00:32:49,400 --> 00:32:50,870
ThirdNine, are you ready?

733
00:32:51,280 --> 00:32:51,980
Okay, come on.

734
00:32:52,000 --> 00:32:52,890
Team, are we ready?

735
00:32:52,910 --> 00:32:53,310
Alright, let's go.

736
00:32:53,330 --> 00:32:54,680
Ready for a detailed shot? Come on.

737
00:32:54,700 --> 00:32:56,070
Alright, kids. Watch.

738
00:32:56,090 --> 00:32:58,210
Watch and learn how it's done.

739
00:32:58,230 --> 00:32:59,870
One day, you'll have to act like they do.

740
00:33:00,580 --> 00:33:02,000
Not today, though.

741
00:33:02,590 --> 00:33:03,260
Capisce?

742
00:33:03,700 --> 00:33:04,340
Jern.

743
00:33:04,360 --> 00:33:05,610
All set? What are we waiting for?

744
00:33:05,730 --> 00:33:07,690
Ugh, I'm calling it!

745
00:33:07,720 --> 00:33:08,900
And...

746
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:10,660
action!

747
00:33:12,800 --> 00:33:14,200
You're worried about something, right?

748
00:33:16,410 --> 00:33:17,190
Mm...

749
00:33:18,440 --> 00:33:19,680
Don't focus on anything else.

750
00:33:20,210 --> 00:33:21,380
Just focus on swimming.

751
00:33:22,960 --> 00:33:24,630
Well, that's all I want to focus on,

752
00:33:24,650 --> 00:33:25,590
but...

753
00:33:26,480 --> 00:33:27,660
I'm also

754
00:33:27,680 --> 00:33:29,420
worried about you.

755
00:33:47,720 --> 00:33:48,550
Cut!

756
00:33:49,220 --> 00:33:50,360
Fabulous!

757
00:33:50,490 --> 00:33:51,560
Fabulous!

758
00:33:52,030 --> 00:33:53,390
Nine, Third, come to me at the monitor.

759
00:33:53,410 --> 00:33:54,670
Yeah, come on. I don't wanna move.

760
00:33:54,690 --> 00:33:55,830
- It's hot. Come on.
- It's good. I like it.

761
00:33:55,850 --> 00:33:56,820
This take feels relaxing.

762
00:33:56,840 --> 00:33:59,720
Yeah, I think
the variations in eye contact

763
00:33:59,740 --> 00:34:01,600
are a lot better than in the workshop.

764
00:34:06,660 --> 00:34:07,980
- That's a print.
- I think...

765
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:10,239
'Cause I'm about to bail.

766
00:34:10,420 --> 00:34:12,320
So the next one is an action scene,

767
00:34:12,340 --> 00:34:14,260
which isn't my job.

768
00:34:14,280 --> 00:34:14,870
I'm heading out

769
00:34:14,889 --> 00:34:16,380
because I've got an event after, okay?

770
00:34:16,400 --> 00:34:17,810
- I'm leaving. Bye, y'all!
- Goodbye.

771
00:34:17,830 --> 00:34:20,270
- Thank you very much.
- A bad example. Taking on overlapping jobs.

772
00:34:20,290 --> 00:34:22,010
- What? Who takes on overlapping jobs?
- You shouldn't be doing that.

773
00:34:22,030 --> 00:34:23,389
I took on that job before this one.

774
00:34:23,409 --> 00:34:24,980
You're the one overlapping.

775
00:34:51,980 --> 00:34:53,920
Can I ask you a straight question?

776
00:34:54,270 --> 00:34:57,220
What are your feelings toward Third?

777
00:34:57,610 --> 00:34:58,790
Are they still the same?

778
00:35:02,260 --> 00:35:03,560
Send in the guards, please.

779
00:35:03,580 --> 00:35:05,150
There's a stalking sasaeng in here.

780
00:35:05,670 --> 00:35:06,620
Keep your focus here.

781
00:35:07,020 --> 00:35:08,500
Think of it as a flower.

782
00:35:08,870 --> 00:35:10,030
One...

783
00:35:10,310 --> 00:35:11,410
Two...

784
00:35:11,600 --> 00:35:12,830
Three...

785
00:35:14,550 --> 00:35:15,960
Only look at me.

786
00:35:18,130 --> 00:35:19,130
Only listen to me.

787
00:35:20,590 --> 00:35:21,500
Stay with me.

788
00:35:21,540 --> 00:35:22,700
How about this?

789
00:35:22,720 --> 00:35:24,500
If you don't want us to fight,

790
00:35:24,520 --> 00:35:26,420
Try to keep a distance from him.

791
00:35:27,380 --> 00:35:28,330
I'm sure...

792
00:35:28,350 --> 00:35:29,510
you wouldn't lie

793
00:35:29,960 --> 00:35:31,380
or hurt me.

794
00:35:31,600 --> 00:35:32,650
Rest assured.

795
00:35:32,920 --> 00:35:34,040
I'll do everything I can

796
00:35:34,060 --> 00:35:35,970
to help you succeed, Nine,

797
00:35:35,990 --> 00:35:38,300
because I'm your fanboy.

798
00:35:43,040 --> 00:35:45,830
Alrighty, come on. Let's get to filming.

799
00:35:45,850 --> 00:35:46,720
Then, for those two,

800
00:35:46,740 --> 00:35:47,840
I'll have them stand over there.

801
00:35:47,860 --> 00:35:48,800
- Mm.
- Like a couple of twinkles.

802
00:35:49,170 --> 00:35:50,540
Alright? They won't
block the punch that way.

803
00:35:50,560 --> 00:35:52,300
Sure. Move the mark so that it...

804
00:35:52,320 --> 00:35:52,740
Sure, sure, sure.

805
00:35:52,760 --> 00:35:53,810
Where am I standing, Jern?

806
00:35:53,830 --> 00:35:54,920
Come on, come on.

807
00:35:55,020 --> 00:35:56,370
Main characters like you boys,

808
00:35:56,390 --> 00:35:58,520
stand right here. You're gonna be stars.

809
00:35:59,280 --> 00:36:00,210
There, there, there.

810
00:36:00,270 --> 00:36:01,320
You'll feel like a twinkle, sweeties.

811
00:36:01,340 --> 00:36:02,190
Just at first.

812
00:36:02,210 --> 00:36:04,040
Once you become famous, bam,

813
00:36:04,060 --> 00:36:05,630
you're gonna shine brighter, like stars.

814
00:36:05,650 --> 00:36:06,070
Alright.

815
00:36:06,090 --> 00:36:07,450
You two, get the marks right.

816
00:36:07,470 --> 00:36:08,700
Pai will come in for the blocking.

817
00:36:08,730 --> 00:36:10,580
- Pai, go ahead.
- I'm gonna go ahead with the briefing.

818
00:36:10,640 --> 00:36:12,220
Alright, action scenes

819
00:36:12,250 --> 00:36:14,000
are my strong suit.

820
00:36:14,020 --> 00:36:15,120
It's easy-peasy.

821
00:36:15,140 --> 00:36:15,750
- Right.
- You two...

822
00:36:15,770 --> 00:36:17,470
stand right on the marks.

823
00:36:17,490 --> 00:36:18,440
And when you punch,

824
00:36:18,590 --> 00:36:20,130
just swing past him like so, bam.

825
00:36:20,160 --> 00:36:21,920
Yeah, and you just flick
in the same direction.

826
00:36:22,290 --> 00:36:22,920
Give it a try.

827
00:36:23,670 --> 00:36:25,170
Swing past him, bam.

828
00:36:25,190 --> 00:36:25,750
Yeah.

829
00:36:25,770 --> 00:36:27,000
And whether you wanna flick,

830
00:36:27,020 --> 00:36:28,750
fall to the ground, or stay standing,

831
00:36:28,770 --> 00:36:30,220
- it's up to you. Go with the flow. Got it?
- Why are you staring at me?

832
00:36:30,250 --> 00:36:32,300
- Look over there!
- And don't pull any method acting on me.

833
00:36:32,320 --> 00:36:33,210
This scene, yeah?

834
00:36:33,230 --> 00:36:35,050
- Right.
- Use your imagination.

835
00:36:35,070 --> 00:36:36,960
- Swinging past his face looks realistic.
- Sure thing.

836
00:36:37,590 --> 00:36:38,400
I say it's easy.

837
00:36:38,420 --> 00:36:39,060
Let's get to filming.

838
00:36:39,080 --> 00:36:39,680
Alright. Come on, kids.

839
00:36:39,700 --> 00:36:41,400
Be on standby, sweeties.

840
00:36:43,010 --> 00:36:43,680
Get the slate ready.

841
00:36:43,830 --> 00:36:44,770
Just a sec.

842
00:36:44,800 --> 00:36:46,140
Right, crew members, keep silent.

843
00:36:46,160 --> 00:36:47,030
Ready, go.

844
00:36:47,050 --> 00:36:48,070
Roll... camera!

845
00:36:48,100 --> 00:36:50,160
- Camera rolling, sound rolling.
- Camera speed!

846
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:53,110
Scene 4, Cut 1, Take 1.

847
00:36:53,130 --> 00:36:53,690
Set!

848
00:36:53,710 --> 00:36:54,720
Alright, set.

849
00:36:55,620 --> 00:36:56,810
And...

850
00:36:57,000 --> 00:36:58,080
action!

851
00:36:58,830 --> 00:36:59,830
Is this...

852
00:37:01,020 --> 00:37:02,610
the promising young shark

853
00:37:02,630 --> 00:37:05,440
Coach praises so much?

854
00:37:09,420 --> 00:37:10,750
All I can see is a fucking loser.

855
00:37:10,770 --> 00:37:11,600
Shut up!

856
00:37:11,620 --> 00:37:12,600
Can't handle some sting?

857
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:16,200
Why are you staring at me?

858
00:37:17,150 --> 00:37:17,920
Angry?

859
00:37:19,190 --> 00:37:20,190
Are you angry?

860
00:37:21,720 --> 00:37:23,280
Or you can't handle the truth I said?

861
00:37:23,620 --> 00:37:25,020
You hate me

862
00:37:25,780 --> 00:37:27,680
because you were
gonna break up with Bas and fall for me?

863
00:37:28,520 --> 00:37:29,480
You!

864
00:37:30,200 --> 00:37:30,680
Ow!

865
00:37:34,950 --> 00:37:36,160
- Whoa!
- Third!

866
00:37:36,610 --> 00:37:37,360
Cut!

867
00:37:37,910 --> 00:37:39,280
Jern, go check on Third!

868
00:37:39,910 --> 00:37:40,720
Was that a real hit?

869
00:37:40,960 --> 00:37:41,670
Third,

870
00:37:42,180 --> 00:37:43,310
did that split your lip?

871
00:37:43,640 --> 00:37:44,100
Let me see.

872
00:37:46,580 --> 00:37:46,990
Wan!

873
00:37:47,010 --> 00:37:47,710
Does it hurt?

874
00:37:47,730 --> 00:37:48,440
You hit him for real?

875
00:37:50,350 --> 00:37:51,520
What went wrong in that briefing?

876
00:37:51,600 --> 00:37:52,960
There aren't any safeguards for him?

877
00:37:55,920 --> 00:37:56,790
That was intentional, wasn't it?

878
00:37:56,810 --> 00:37:57,400
Sunny...

879
00:37:59,630 --> 00:38:00,630
I...

880
00:38:01,520 --> 00:38:02,320
I'm sorry.

881
00:38:02,340 --> 00:38:03,320
I didn't mean to.

882
00:38:03,550 --> 00:38:04,560
What a shitty thing to say!

883
00:38:05,550 --> 00:38:06,540
Just because you said you didn't mean it,

884
00:38:06,560 --> 00:38:07,480
you think it's over?

885
00:38:08,290 --> 00:38:09,800
Well, he said he didn't mean to.

886
00:38:09,820 --> 00:38:10,760
It was an accident.

887
00:38:11,260 --> 00:38:12,110
Fine.

888
00:38:13,300 --> 00:38:14,490
Then, all of you here,

889
00:38:14,510 --> 00:38:15,440
how are you gonna pay

890
00:38:15,600 --> 00:38:16,790
for Third getting hurt?

891
00:38:18,540 --> 00:38:20,520
I saw you rehearse that briefing for ages.

892
00:38:20,600 --> 00:38:21,920
Why did you still mess up?

893
00:38:22,260 --> 00:38:23,320
What happened to Third

894
00:38:23,340 --> 00:38:24,680
was a serious hit, Pai.

895
00:38:24,950 --> 00:38:27,080
VE ENT can sue you all.

896
00:38:27,100 --> 00:38:28,630
I'll sue you all.

897
00:38:29,210 --> 00:38:30,530
Ms. Sunny, how about...

898
00:38:30,550 --> 00:38:31,360
I...

899
00:38:31,380 --> 00:38:33,320
First of all, I apologize on his behalf.

900
00:38:33,530 --> 00:38:34,760
It was an accident.

901
00:38:34,880 --> 00:38:36,310
Please don't take it to court.

902
00:38:36,330 --> 00:38:38,560
I think we can settle this.

903
00:38:38,730 --> 00:38:39,610
Sure.

904
00:38:39,670 --> 00:38:41,100
Go on. I'm listening.

905
00:38:41,120 --> 00:38:42,000
Sunny,

906
00:38:42,520 --> 00:38:43,920
no one is being sued.

907
00:38:44,510 --> 00:38:45,510
That's not possible, Third.

908
00:38:45,530 --> 00:38:46,060
Does it hurt?

909
00:38:46,080 --> 00:38:47,120
I'm okay.

910
00:38:50,500 --> 00:38:51,810
Then, we're taking a break.

911
00:38:52,260 --> 00:38:53,300
He needs to rest.

912
00:38:54,690 --> 00:38:55,270
Uh...

913
00:38:55,430 --> 00:38:56,650
But... But Miss,

914
00:38:56,670 --> 00:38:59,280
we're already going over schedule.

915
00:38:59,900 --> 00:39:01,080
I don't care.

916
00:39:01,350 --> 00:39:03,180
If you're smart enough, figure it out.

917
00:39:03,940 --> 00:39:04,670
Come on.

918
00:39:07,620 --> 00:39:08,720
Jern, you idiot!

919
00:39:08,740 --> 00:39:09,950
You really asked her that!

920
00:39:09,970 --> 00:39:11,040
Why the hell did you?!

921
00:39:11,060 --> 00:39:12,220
Just to get roasted?!

922
00:39:12,260 --> 00:39:14,380
I'm the director,
but you didn't even help.

923
00:39:14,400 --> 00:39:16,270
What kind of assistant are you?

924
00:39:16,330 --> 00:39:17,560
You assist in making it worse.

925
00:39:18,310 --> 00:39:19,710
Let's just use...

926
00:39:20,160 --> 00:39:21,140
the take with the real hit.

927
00:39:21,160 --> 00:39:22,430
That works. So realistic.

928
00:39:23,200 --> 00:39:25,400
You, shoot some B-roll footage and wrap up.

929
00:39:36,010 --> 00:39:36,840
Cher...

930
00:39:36,860 --> 00:39:38,560
I wanna check on Third!

931
00:39:39,060 --> 00:39:40,210
Not now.

932
00:39:41,330 --> 00:39:43,000
But I want to apologize to him.

933
00:39:44,150 --> 00:39:45,520
Not right now, Wan.

934
00:39:46,420 --> 00:39:47,690
Right now, everyone is raging.

935
00:39:47,710 --> 00:39:48,720
If you go, you'll only lose.

936
00:39:49,320 --> 00:39:51,030
This is gonna be a big deal.

937
00:39:51,050 --> 00:39:53,430
We have to talk to Wut
and fix it afterwards.

938
00:39:53,740 --> 00:39:55,520
But I really didn't mean to, Cher.

939
00:39:56,040 --> 00:39:58,000
They don't care
whether you meant to or not.

940
00:40:00,220 --> 00:40:01,220
They're gonna use

941
00:40:01,240 --> 00:40:03,280
this whole thing to crush you.

942
00:40:11,770 --> 00:40:12,460
Pitch,

943
00:40:13,320 --> 00:40:14,760
can we file a lawsuit?

944
00:40:15,190 --> 00:40:16,280
What can we do?

945
00:40:16,680 --> 00:40:18,230
Should we talk to the legal department?

946
00:40:18,260 --> 00:40:19,940
What are we gonna get out of this

947
00:40:20,330 --> 00:40:21,480
if we take this further?

948
00:40:22,130 --> 00:40:23,630
Something's gotta be done, Pitch.

949
00:40:23,650 --> 00:40:25,040
Our actor was punched.

950
00:40:25,640 --> 00:40:26,560
Or...

951
00:40:26,960 --> 00:40:28,090
should we leak the vid?

952
00:40:28,600 --> 00:40:29,720
That'll screw everyone equally.

953
00:40:29,740 --> 00:40:31,130
Stop this stupidity.

954
00:40:31,880 --> 00:40:33,510
If it goes south, it goes south.

955
00:40:34,520 --> 00:40:35,920
But if all goes well,

956
00:40:36,310 --> 00:40:38,250
that Wan kid will get even more clout.

957
00:40:41,040 --> 00:40:42,920
They're definitely
taking this matter to North.

958
00:40:43,050 --> 00:40:44,800
I will take this matter to North.

959
00:40:46,010 --> 00:40:47,390
Now, we can finally...

960
00:40:47,840 --> 00:40:48,930
squeeze that brat out.

961
00:40:49,220 --> 00:40:51,410
Should we beat them to it
with a statement?

962
00:40:51,840 --> 00:40:52,840
Say it's an accident.

963
00:40:53,100 --> 00:40:54,880
That's worse than just being defensive.

964
00:40:55,520 --> 00:40:56,690
I believe North already knows.

965
00:40:57,110 --> 00:40:58,870
It now comes down
to what he's gonna do to us.

966
00:40:58,890 --> 00:40:59,960
But right now...

967
00:41:00,330 --> 00:41:02,420
we have to contain
this matter from leaking outside,

968
00:41:02,740 --> 00:41:04,080
or else it'll be even harder to fix.

969
00:41:08,690 --> 00:41:10,660
[Cher, the video of me
punching Third is all over X]

970
00:41:14,030 --> 00:41:15,320
It's too late, Wut.

971
00:41:22,780 --> 00:41:23,230
Wan!

972
00:41:23,250 --> 00:41:24,110
You hit him for real?

973
00:41:24,140 --> 00:41:25,450
What went wrong in that briefing?

974
00:41:25,470 --> 00:41:26,870
- There aren't any safeguards for him?
- We're doomed...

975
00:41:27,700 --> 00:41:29,100
Jern, go check on Third!

976
00:41:29,120 --> 00:41:29,880
Did that split your lip?

977
00:41:42,380 --> 00:41:43,490
You did this?

978
00:41:45,320 --> 00:41:47,320
Well, where did you get the video?

979
00:41:48,930 --> 00:41:51,030
I have eyes and ears on set.

980
00:41:53,320 --> 00:41:55,140
Any move that creates buzz

981
00:41:55,160 --> 00:41:56,240
is good for the series.

982
00:41:56,770 --> 00:41:58,910
No harm to you, since
you have nothing to do with this.

983
00:42:00,220 --> 00:42:01,670
If there's drama,

984
00:42:01,910 --> 00:42:03,170
there's fame.

985
00:42:04,810 --> 00:42:05,410
Uh...

986
00:42:07,040 --> 00:42:07,830
I mean...

987
00:42:09,530 --> 00:42:12,120
what if it creates more buzz for Wan?

988
00:42:13,810 --> 00:42:14,810
Well...

989
00:42:15,330 --> 00:42:17,830
Lucky for him, I guess?

990
00:42:24,520 --> 00:42:25,370
[#DivingDeeperIntoTheSet]

991
00:42:25,390 --> 00:42:26,820
[I knew it; rushing down
to help a fan was for clout]

992
00:42:26,840 --> 00:42:27,920
[He punched my baby boy? I'm cursing him!]

993
00:42:37,660 --> 00:42:39,000
[Cher]

994
00:42:42,680 --> 00:42:43,800
Hello, Cher?

995
00:42:45,080 --> 00:42:46,380
Keep still, Wan.

996
00:42:46,400 --> 00:42:47,870
The company will sort this out.

997
00:42:48,790 --> 00:42:50,530
How am I supposed to keep still, Cher?

998
00:42:50,930 --> 00:42:51,820
Just do.

999
00:42:52,000 --> 00:42:53,160
Have faith in us.

1000
00:42:53,430 --> 00:42:54,260
You, stop scrolling

1001
00:42:54,280 --> 00:42:55,100
and go to bed.

1002
00:42:58,420 --> 00:42:59,010
Alright.

1003
00:43:16,120 --> 00:43:17,790
[third.tharit]

1004
00:43:33,560 --> 00:43:35,280
[wan_ashawin]

1005
00:43:41,110 --> 00:43:42,220
Hello, you...

1006
00:43:42,900 --> 00:43:43,530
What?

1007
00:43:46,610 --> 00:43:47,640
I'm sorry.

1008
00:43:47,990 --> 00:43:49,750
I didn't mean to.

1009
00:43:51,750 --> 00:43:54,280
Honestly, I'm not calling to make excuses.

1010
00:43:55,120 --> 00:43:55,720
It's just...

1011
00:43:56,280 --> 00:43:58,060
I miscalculated the reach.

1012
00:43:58,180 --> 00:43:59,900
I didn't think it would hit you.

1013
00:44:00,410 --> 00:44:02,030
"Rewarded good with evil."

1014
00:44:02,420 --> 00:44:03,800
I helped someone but got injured?

1015
00:44:08,870 --> 00:44:10,230
I'm sorry.

1016
00:44:11,830 --> 00:44:13,310
Chew me out however you want.

1017
00:44:14,190 --> 00:44:15,120
I yield!

1018
00:44:15,150 --> 00:44:16,210
So you want me to chew you out

1019
00:44:16,230 --> 00:44:18,390
because that punch
was actually intentional?

1020
00:44:18,570 --> 00:44:19,570
No... you.

1021
00:44:19,590 --> 00:44:20,630
Are you crazy?

1022
00:44:20,790 --> 00:44:22,230
Why would I punch you on purpose?

1023
00:44:23,050 --> 00:44:24,500
So why do you want me to chew you out?

1024
00:44:27,810 --> 00:44:28,610
Well...

1025
00:44:28,630 --> 00:44:29,860
I'm being chewed out so badly

1026
00:44:29,880 --> 00:44:31,430
that I'm trending.

1027
00:44:33,080 --> 00:44:34,590
But well...I deserved it.

1028
00:44:35,110 --> 00:44:36,400
I hurt someone's fave.

1029
00:44:37,660 --> 00:44:39,040
Don't you think it's strange?

1030
00:44:39,790 --> 00:44:41,700
Grumbling to the person you punched?

1031
00:44:42,040 --> 00:44:42,910
It is.

1032
00:44:44,020 --> 00:44:44,990
Honestly...

1033
00:44:45,010 --> 00:44:46,690
I feel so bad

1034
00:44:46,940 --> 00:44:49,310
because you're an actor.

1035
00:44:49,820 --> 00:44:51,800
You make a living with your face.

1036
00:44:54,340 --> 00:44:54,970
I'm so...

1037
00:44:54,990 --> 00:44:55,850
Don't mind it.

1038
00:44:56,510 --> 00:44:57,150
Huh?

1039
00:45:07,740 --> 00:45:09,510
I meant, you need to take responsibility.

1040
00:45:12,600 --> 00:45:14,820
If you can do that, I'll forgive you.

1041
00:45:15,640 --> 00:45:16,960
How do I take responsibility?

1042
00:45:24,370 --> 00:45:25,470
[The footage was part
of a crucial scene in the pilot shoot

1043
00:45:25,490 --> 00:45:26,590
and was only a rehearsal filmed
under the close supervision of the staff;

1044
00:45:26,610 --> 00:45:27,430
as the producer, we apologize
if the unauthorized disclosure of the video

1045
00:45:27,450 --> 00:45:28,380
caused any discomfort
or misunderstanding regarding the actor]

1046
00:45:34,100 --> 00:45:35,410
[NPY]

1047
00:45:35,970 --> 00:45:37,850
That little statement was not okay.

1048
00:45:38,440 --> 00:45:40,020
Even though it was an accident,

1049
00:45:40,080 --> 00:45:41,180
Third was genuinely hurt.

1050
00:45:41,200 --> 00:45:42,440
This is damaging to me.

1051
00:45:42,550 --> 00:45:44,680
From the start, I told you to fire Wan.

1052
00:45:45,060 --> 00:45:47,300
I believe you have something to consider.

1053
00:45:47,960 --> 00:45:50,320
I'm considering not letting
Nine and Third continue with this project.

1054
00:45:50,440 --> 00:45:52,080
Is it really that big of a deal?

1055
00:45:56,820 --> 00:45:58,440
You asked if we could remove the boy?

1056
00:45:58,710 --> 00:46:01,870
I stand by what I said.
I can find him a new project.

1057
00:46:02,300 --> 00:46:03,220
Honestly, though,

1058
00:46:03,250 --> 00:46:05,930
throwing the million baht you spent
on the pilot down the drain,

1059
00:46:05,980 --> 00:46:07,070
are you seriously doing that?

1060
00:46:07,090 --> 00:46:08,000
It's just a million-ish.

1061
00:46:08,020 --> 00:46:09,330
I can cover it.

1062
00:46:09,350 --> 00:46:10,950
If money isn't a problem,

1063
00:46:11,040 --> 00:46:13,310
you need to clear Wan's name,

1064
00:46:13,340 --> 00:46:14,610
because if he quits right now,

1065
00:46:15,250 --> 00:46:16,660
people will think Wan's in the wrong.

1066
00:46:16,720 --> 00:46:17,850
Well, he is!

1067
00:46:17,870 --> 00:46:19,440
What fucking names
do you want me to clear?!

1068
00:46:20,070 --> 00:46:21,600
I don't think
Wan's that much in the wrong.

1069
00:46:21,810 --> 00:46:23,760
No? Are you sure about that?

1070
00:46:23,780 --> 00:46:25,200
Assault isn't wrong?

1071
00:46:25,350 --> 00:46:26,400
How about this?

1072
00:46:26,530 --> 00:46:27,390
Just put it out there

1073
00:46:27,410 --> 00:46:29,290
that Wan miscued and punched Third.

1074
00:46:30,150 --> 00:46:31,250
I'm dying to know

1075
00:46:31,530 --> 00:46:32,730
what netizens think.

1076
00:46:32,860 --> 00:46:35,100
So now, the production team
is at fault, isn't it?

1077
00:46:35,670 --> 00:46:36,970
This was careless filming.

1078
00:46:37,450 --> 00:46:38,500
An action scene

1079
00:46:38,520 --> 00:46:40,190
needs an action director,

1080
00:46:40,210 --> 00:46:41,560
even if it's only one scene.

1081
00:46:41,800 --> 00:46:43,200
That means...

1082
00:46:43,220 --> 00:46:44,560
you're at fault, right, North?

1083
00:46:45,860 --> 00:46:47,090
What a clown.

1084
00:46:47,110 --> 00:46:49,790
You realize you're reaching
so fucking far that you don't make sense?!

1085
00:46:49,810 --> 00:46:50,960
I'm only stating the facts,

1086
00:46:50,980 --> 00:46:52,000
unlike you,

1087
00:46:52,020 --> 00:46:53,090
who always tries to get the kid fired.

1088
00:46:53,180 --> 00:46:54,650
I've seen what Wan did wrong

1089
00:46:54,670 --> 00:46:55,670
twice now.

1090
00:46:55,700 --> 00:46:57,460
I insist that if you remove Wan,

1091
00:46:57,810 --> 00:46:59,750
the company has to release
a statement dismissing him

1092
00:46:59,770 --> 00:47:01,870
and acknowledge the mistake
on the production team's part.

1093
00:47:03,470 --> 00:47:04,950
But if you can't do that...

1094
00:47:05,240 --> 00:47:06,240
I'll take this to court

1095
00:47:06,560 --> 00:47:08,180
and state that
the production team was at fault

1096
00:47:08,200 --> 00:47:09,330
for not taking good care of my actor.

1097
00:47:10,510 --> 00:47:11,580
That's enough.

1098
00:47:13,260 --> 00:47:14,180
Enough...

1099
00:47:15,330 --> 00:47:17,290
Aren't we in this as business partners?

1100
00:47:18,170 --> 00:47:19,700
How long is this going to go on?

1101
00:47:20,140 --> 00:47:20,890
Like...

1102
00:47:21,830 --> 00:47:24,080
if there's drama,

1103
00:47:24,100 --> 00:47:26,810
isn't that free publicity, guys?

1104
00:47:27,650 --> 00:47:28,650
A win for me,

1105
00:47:28,670 --> 00:47:29,460
for you,

1106
00:47:29,480 --> 00:47:30,780
and for you.

1107
00:47:30,880 --> 00:47:31,990
Yeah!

1108
00:47:32,700 --> 00:47:35,630
So shouldn't we
solve the problem at its root?

1109
00:47:37,540 --> 00:47:38,690
Guys, how about this?

1110
00:47:38,710 --> 00:47:39,740
I think...

1111
00:47:41,100 --> 00:47:42,620
we should generate buzz

1112
00:47:44,080 --> 00:47:45,550
about the male lead and the antagonist

1113
00:47:45,570 --> 00:47:47,360
not being close at all in real life.

1114
00:47:47,610 --> 00:47:48,290
Think about it.

1115
00:47:48,310 --> 00:47:50,400
How invested would the viewers be?

1116
00:47:51,550 --> 00:47:52,440
Huh, silence.

1117
00:47:53,380 --> 00:47:54,960
Alright, I'll help you settle this.

1118
00:47:55,770 --> 00:47:58,070
I already have a promotional project planned.

1119
00:47:58,270 --> 00:47:59,600
I will bring the boys

1120
00:47:59,620 --> 00:48:00,510
together.

1121
00:48:01,050 --> 00:48:01,680
No.

